# Third-Party OS & Runtime Licenses

The Script Language Container is distributed as `lc-rs.tar.gz`, built from the
root `Dockerfile`. That tarball carries a curated staged tree, not a flattened
distribution root filesystem: only the Debian 13 (trixie) runtime libraries a
UDF actually needs are `cp -L`'d out of the `debian:trixie-slim` staging stage
into `/slc` — glibc with its NSS/resolver modules and loader, `libgcc_s` /
`libstdc++`, `ca-certificates`, `tzdata`, OpenSSL 3 with its provider modules,
and the `zlib` / `bzip2` / `zstd` compression libraries. This file reproduces
the licenses and provides the source offer for those staged libraries.

It is complementary to `THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md`, which (via `cargo about`) covers
only the Rust crate graph statically linked into the `exaudfclient` binary.

**No copyleft propagation.** Every component below is an unmodified upstream
binary shipped as a separate file. glibc is LGPL-2.1; `libstdc++`/`libgcc` carry
the GCC Runtime Library Exception. Nothing here propagates its license to
`exaudfclient` or to user-authored UDFs.

This file is generated by `dist/generate-licenses.sh` (see that script);
license texts are rendered by `cargo about` from its embedded SPDX data and are
therefore not committed to the repository.

## Staged libraries (Debian 13 / trixie)

| Library file(s) | Source package | SPDX license |
|------------------|-----------------|--------------|
| `libc.so.6`, `libm.so.6`, `ld-linux-*.so.*`, `libnss_files.so.2`, `libnss_dns.so.2`, `libresolv.so.2` | `glibc` | LGPL-2.1 |
| `libstdc++.so.6`, `libgcc_s.so.1` | `gcc-14` | GPL-3.0-only WITH GCC-exception-3.1 |
| `libssl.so.3`, `libcrypto.so.3`, `ossl-modules/legacy.so`, `engines-3/{afalg,loader_attic,padlock}.so` | `openssl` | Apache-2.0 |
| `libz.so.1` | `zlib` | Zlib |
| `libzstd.so.1` | `libzstd` | BSD-3-Clause |
| `libbz2.so.1` | `bzip2` | bzip2-1.0.6 |
| `ca-certificates` bundle | `ca-certificates` | MPL-2.0 AND MIT |
| `tzdata` (zoneinfo database) | `tzdata` | Public-Domain |

`tzdata` is public domain and carries no reproduction obligation. The OpenSSL
project's `NOTICE` is satisfied by the Apache-2.0 text reproduced below.

## Written offer of corresponding source

For the LGPL-2.1 and GPL-3.0 components above, the corresponding source is the
unmodified upstream source, available for **three (3) years** from the date of
distribution of this container:

- **glibc, gcc-14, openssl, zlib, libzstd, bzip2, ca-certificates, tzdata** —
  Debian 13 (trixie) source packages, archived at
  <https://snapshot.debian.org> and mirrored at <https://sources.debian.org>.

A copy of the corresponding source can also be requested through the project
repository at <https://github.com/exasol-labs/language-container-rs> (open an
issue); requests are honored for the three-year period above.

